# Architecture Rules

- Maintain strict Clean Architecture boundaries:
  - `CalendarWidget.Core` has ZERO external dependencies. Never add project references or EF Core/WPF packages to Core.
  - `CalendarWidget.Presentation` depends only on `CalendarWidget.Core`. It must NEVER reference `CalendarWidget.Infrastructure`.
  - `CalendarWidget.Infrastructure` implements interfaces from `Core`. Never reference Presentation.
  - `CalendarWidget.App` wires everything together via dependency injection.
- UI ViewModels must never access EF Core `DbContext` directly. Always use repository interfaces (`ICalendarEventRepository`, `INoteRepository`).
- Domain logic belongs in `Core`, not in ViewModels or UI code-behind.
